dence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Illinois' governor's race is a rematch of 2022, when incumbent JB Pritzker, a Democrat, defeated Darren Bailey by roughly twelve points. Pritzker is seeking a third term with a dominant financial position, outspending Bailey's campaign about twenty-five to one, and the state's partisan lean favors Democrats by about six points. Every major race rating places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nPolling has been sparse but consistent: two surveys, including one from early October 2026, show Pritzker leading by twenty points among likely voters. Prediction markets price his chances at roughly ninety-five percent. The two met in their only debate in mid-October, clashing over taxes and national politics, with no sign the race has tightened. Barring an unexpected shift, Pritzker appears positioned for a comfortable win, with the main question being the size of his margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026